### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not scored — zero verified public benchmarks (self-exclusion rule). Best available evidence is qualitative: vendor positioning as the platform's flagship for coding + Computer Use, an 8x credit multiplier implying a frontier-class cost structure, and unverified community reports of strong desktop-automation results alongside heavy credit consumption and task-abandonment complaints.

